orld record in the process. At the Worlds, held in Melbourne, Ulmer had defeated Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/106850"} "Katie Mactier"] " in the final. In qualifying in Athina, Ulmer placed first with Mactier second and Zijlaard-van Moorsel third, all three bettering the previous world record. But Ulmer’s time was 3:26.400 on the fast Athina track, leading Mactier by the huge margin of over 3½ seconds. Ulmer dominated the event throughout. In her first round race, she came close to overtaking Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/90486"} "Olga Slyusareva"] ", and in the final defeated Mactier again, this time by over three seconds with another world record of 3:24.537. Van Moorsel finished third in the last competitive race of her career."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13248"} "Sarah Ulmer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "3:26.400 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "3:27.444 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "3:24.537 (1 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106850"} "Katie Mactier"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "3:29.945 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "3:28.095 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "3:27.650 (2 h1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13253"} "Leontien Zijlaard-van Moorsel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", 